# -----------------------------------------------------
# Monitors — laptop
# -----------------------------------------------------
# config.conf does `source=~/.config/mango/monitors.conf` unconditionally, and
# only ##class.desktop / ##class.work existed, so on a laptop that source
# pointed at nothing. mango tolerates a missing source silently, which is worse
# than erroring: it looks fine right up until you add a rule here and wonder
# why it has no effect.
#
# CONNECTOR NAMES ARE NOT STABLE. They change when the driver changes and when
# cables move ports. Check the current set with:
#     mmsg get all-monitors
#
# The internal panel deliberately has no monitorrule: with one built-in display
# the EDID-preferred mode is the right answer, and hardcoding a mode here is how
# you end up locked to the wrong refresh rate after a driver update. Add rules
# only for external outputs you actually dock to.
#
# Example, if you dock:
#     monitorrule=DP-1,0.5,1,tile,0,1,2560,1440,144
#     (name, mfact, nmaster, layout, rotate, scale, width, height, refresh)

# No rules: single internal panel, EDID-preferred mode.
#
# No game-placement windowrule either — see the note in gaming.conf. Pinning
# games to a monitor only makes sense with more than one, and a rule naming an
# output that does not exist silently swallows the window.
